OL,3,GNEWSAHospice care eases pressure on
OL,4,Afamilies, mum says
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe mother of a six-year-old boy says
OL,7,Fhospice care has been "incredibly
OL,8,Fimportant" for her family, and has
OL,9,Fcalled on the government to prioritise
OL,10,Fsupporting the services.
OL,12,FKit, from Tunbridge Wells in Kent, has
OL,13,Fepilepsy, motor dysfunction and is
OL,14,Fpartially blind after a seizure when he
OL,15,Fwas 18 months old damaged his brain.
OL,17,FHis mother, Katherine, is now calling
OL,18,Ffor hospices to be better supported,
OL,19,Fafter Kit lost services due to the
OL,20,Fstruggles charities face.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,323,320,200,140,0,100
